Description: Disable len() assert in rust_bindgen.gni for older GN versions
 Debian's generate-ninja package does not yet include the len() builtin
 function. Comment out the assert that uses it, as it is only a safety
 check and the code works correctly without it.
 .
 Based on Debian Chromium's trixie/gn-len.patch by Andres Salomon.
 See Debian bug #1127702 for the generate-ninja update request.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-02-15

diff --git a/build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni b/build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni
index 9fd2dce..86d3d43 100644
--- a/build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni
+++ b/build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ template("rust_bindgen") {
   # Calculate `_generated_bindings_rs`.
   _bindgen_outputs = get_target_outputs(":$_rust_bindgen_generator_target_name")
   _bindgen_rs_outputs = filter_include(_bindgen_outputs, [ "*.rs" ])
-  assert(len(_bindgen_rs_outputs) == 1)
+#  assert(len(_bindgen_rs_outputs) == 1)
   _generated_bindings_rs = _bindgen_rs_outputs[0]

   rust_static_library(target_name) {
